TTYCHATTER C COMMAND-LINE WALKTHROUGH
=====================================

This walkthrough guides a first-time user from an empty setup to both the
traditional file workflow and the line-oriented interactive workflow.

1. Build
--------

    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get install build-essential pkg-config libcurl4-openssl-dev libjson-c-dev ca-certificates gnupg

    cd c
    make

Check the binary:

    ./ttychatter --version
    ./ttychatter --help

2. Try demo mode
----------------

Demo mode does not use the network.

    ./ttychatter --demo --models
    ./ttychatter --demo --test-model demo/large-context

3. Try file-in/file-out mode
----------------------------

    cat > first.txt
    Explain the purpose of demo mode.
    ^D

    ./ttychatter --demo --loopback first.txt session.log

Open the session:

    less session.log

4. Try interactive mode
-----------------------

    ./ttychatter --demo --interactive session.log

Then type:

    :help
    hello from interactive demo mode
    :memory
    :quit

Colon commands are local ttychatter commands.  They are not sent to the model.

5. Store an OpenRouter API key
------------------------------

Encrypted storage:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

Environment variable alternative:

    export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="your-key"

6. Get models
-------------

    ./ttychatter --update-models
    ./ttychatter --models --search free
    ./ttychatter --models --model-type routers
    ./ttychatter --models --sort context

7. Bookmark a model
-------------------

    ./ttychatter --favorite-model openrouter/auto
    ./ttychatter --favorites

8. Test a model
---------------

    ./ttychatter --test-model openrouter/auto

9. Real file workflow
---------------------

    cat > first.txt
    Explain router models versus fixed models.
    ^D

    ./ttychatter -m openrouter/auto first.txt session.log

Continue the session:

    cat > followup.txt
    Give me a shorter explanation.
    ^D

    ./ttychatter -m openrouter/auto followup.txt session.log

10. Attach files
----------------

    ./ttychatter -a notes.txt -a image.png question.txt session.log

11. Use loopback
----------------

    ./ttychatter --loopback question.txt session.log | tee latest-response.txt
